obs-server (0~git20260313.eec7f37-1obs11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian testing packaging for the OBS server stack.
  * Build against the project-local Ruby 3.4 and bundled gem packages.
  * Drop the hard mod_xforward requirement from the Apache vhost template.
  * Treat Diff::LibXDiff as optional on Debian because the backend loads it
    via eval.
  * Drop the libsolv-perl versioned dependency to match Debian package
    metadata.
  * Replace the heavy obs-api-testsuite-deps build dependency with the
    minimal Ruby/Node precompile stack.
  * Force UTF-8 Ruby defaults during the build and swagger generation.
  * Rewrite src/api/bin shebangs to /usr/bin/ruby3.4 for Debian testing.
  * Add tzdata for assets precompile and Rails runtime timezone lookup.
  * Switch Debian packaging to /etc/default/obs-server and keep
    /etc/sysconfig/obs-server as a compatibility fallback.
  * Run obsstoragesetup with bash because the upstream script uses bashisms.
  * Replace obsapisetup.service with a Debian-native API/database bootstrap
    helper instead of the SUSE appliance setup script.
  * Install /etc/default/obs-server as a real config file instead of a
    directory wrapper.
  * Regenerate API config/secret.key during install and autosetup when it is
    missing.
  * Pull required backend daemons into obsapisetup.service before running
    writeconfiguration.

 -- hao <hao@local>  Sun, 15 Mar 2026 15:00:00 +0800
